hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1098","Chapter on keeping horses tied for battle, 1137 - Muhammad ibn Yahya and al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us; they said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection. And Ibn Yahya said: forever, until the Day of Resurrection."
